{"result": "{\n    \"title\": \"PACIENTES: Nutritional Support Community\",\n    \"summary\": \"The PACIENTES community encompasses a diverse group of individuals facing various medical conditions that require specialized nutritional support and dietary management. This community includes patients with chronic diseases, eating disorders, and those needing enteral or parenteral nutrition, highlighting the interconnectedness of their health challenges and nutritional needs.\",\n    \"rating\": 8.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is high due to the critical health conditions faced by the individuals in this community, which necessitate comprehensive nutritional interventions.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Diverse Nutritional Needs of PACIENTES\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The PACIENTES community includes individuals with a wide range of medical conditions, each requiring tailored nutritional support. This diversity highlights the complexity of managing nutritional needs across different health issues, such as chronic respiratory diseases, gastrointestinal disorders, and eating disorders. For instance, patients with conditions like EPOC and cystic fibrosis often face significant nutritional challenges that require specialized dietary management to ensure adequate intake and prevent complications [Data: Entities (17); Relationships (294, 586, 650)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Critical Role of Enteral and Parenteral Nutrition\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Enteral and parenteral nutrition are vital components of care for many individuals in the PACIENTES community. Patients who cannot meet their nutritional needs through oral intake due to severe malnutrition or medical complications often rely on these forms of nutrition. For example, patients with severe malnutrition may require parenteral nutrition when enteral routes are not feasible, emphasizing the importance of these interventions in their recovery [Data: Entities (17); Relationships (473, 445)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Impact of Eating Disorders on Nutritional Status\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Eating disorders, such as anorexia nervosa, significantly affect the nutritional status of individuals within the PACIENTES community. These patients often require specialized nutritional support and psychotherapy to address both their psychological and dietary needs. The interplay between mental health and nutrition is crucial, as effective treatment for eating disorders must incorporate comprehensive dietary education and support [Data: Entities (8928, 8892); Relationships (3467, 517)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Challenges in Managing Dysphagia\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Dysphagia, or difficulty swallowing, is a common issue among patients in the PACIENTES community, particularly those with neurological disorders or after certain surgeries. This condition necessitates specialized care and often requires enteral nutrition to ensure adequate nutrient intake. The Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofaríngea plays a critical role in providing tailored interventions for these patients, highlighting the need for specialized services in managing swallowing disorders [Data: Entities (23); Relationships (423)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Importance of Nutritional Assessment and Monitoring\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Regular nutritional assessment and monitoring are essential for patients in the PACIENTES community to identify and address nutritional deficiencies early. Tools such as the NUTRIC SCORE and periodic densitometries are utilized to evaluate the nutritional status and bone health of patients, particularly those receiving parenteral nutrition. This proactive approach is vital for optimizing patient outcomes and preventing complications related to malnutrition [Data: Entities (561, 500); Relationships (610, 496)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Family and Caregivers\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Family members, particularly parents of children with food allergies, play a crucial role in ensuring safe nutrition for their loved ones. The involvement of caregivers is essential in managing dietary restrictions and providing support for patients with complex nutritional needs. This highlights the importance of education and resources for families to effectively navigate the challenges associated with dietary management [Data: Entities (6798); Relationships (618)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Interconnectedness of Medical Conditions\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The PACIENTES community illustrates the interconnectedness of various medical conditions and their impact on nutritional needs. For example, patients with chronic respiratory diseases may also experience complications such as diabetes or malnutrition, necessitating a comprehensive approach to their care. This interconnectedness underscores the need for multidisciplinary teams to address the complex health challenges faced by these individuals [Data: Entities (23); Relationships (570, 586)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Emerging Needs for Specialized Nutritional Products\",\n            \"explanation\": \"As the PACIENTES community continues to grow, there is an increasing demand for specialized nutritional products tailored to the unique needs of patients with specific conditions. This includes commercially adapted food options for individuals with dysphagia and enteral nutrition formulas designed for patients with metabolic disorders. The development and availability of these products are crucial for enhancing patient care and improving dietary compliance [Data: Entities (1587, 1586); Relationships (470, 469)].\"\n        }\n    ]\n}", "input": "\nYou are an AI assistant that helps a human analyst to perform general information discovery. Information discovery is the process of identifying and assessing relevant information associated with certain entities (e.g., organizations and individuals) within a network.\n\n# Goal\nWrite a comprehensive report of a community, given a list of entities that belong to the community as well as their relationships and optional associated claims. The report will be used to inform decision-makers about information associated with the community and their potential impact. The content of this report includes an overview of the community's key entities, their legal compliance, technical capabilities, reputation, and noteworthy claims.\n\n# Report Structure\n\nThe report should include the following sections:\n\n- TITLE: community's name that represents its key entities - title should be short but specific. When possible, include representative named entities in the title.\n- SUMMARY: An executive summary of the community's overall structure, how its entities are related to each other, and significant information associated with its entities.\n- IMPACT SEVERITY RATING: a float score between 0-10 that represents the severity of IMPACT posed by entities within the community.  IMPACT is the scored importance of a community.\n- RATING EXPLANATION: Give a single sentence explanation of the IMPACT severity rating.\n- DETAILED FINDINGS: A list of 5-10 key insights about the community. Each insight should have a short summary followed by multiple paragraphs of explanatory text grounded according to the grounding rules below. Be comprehensive.\n\nReturn output as a well-formed JSON-formatted string with the following format:\n    {{\n        \"title\": <report_title>,\n        \"summary\": <executive_summary>,\n        \"rating\": <impact_severity_rating>,\n        \"rating_explanation\": <rating_explanation>,\n        \"findings\": [\n            {{\n                \"summary\":<insight_1_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_1_explanation>\n            }},\n            {{\n                \"summary\":<insight_2_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_2_explanation>\n            }}\n        ]\n    }}\n\n# Grounding Rules\n\nPoints supported by data should list their data references as follows:\n\n\"This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: <dataset name> (record ids); <dataset name> (record ids)].\"\n\nDo not list more than 5 record ids in a single reference. Instead, list the top 5 most relevant record ids and add \"+more\" to indicate that there are more.\n\nFor example:\n\"Person X is the owner of Company Y and subject to many allegations of wrongdoing [Data: Reports (1), Entities (5, 7); Relationships (23); Claims (7, 2, 34, 64, 46, +more)].\"\n\nwhere 1, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, 46, and 64 represent the id (not the index) of the relevant data record.\n\nDo not include information where the supporting evidence for it is not provided.\n\n\n# Example Input\n-----------\nText:\n\nEntities\n\nid,entity,description\n5,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n6,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is an organization that is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n\nRelationships\n\nid,source,target,description\n37,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n38,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n39,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,The Unity March is taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n40,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,TRIBUNE SPOTLIGHT,Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity march taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n41,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,BAILEY ASADI,Bailey Asadi is speaking at Verdant Oasis Plaza about the march\n43,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,UNITY MARCH,Harmony Assembly is organizing the Unity March\n\nOutput:\n{{\n    \"title\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza and Unity March\",\n    \"summary\": \"The community revolves around the Verdant Oasis Plaza, which is the location of the Unity March. The plaza has relationships with the Harmony Assembly, Unity March, and Tribune Spotlight, all of which are associated with the march event.\",\n    \"rating\": 5.0,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is moderate due to the potential for unrest or conflict during the Unity March.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza as the central location\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza is the central entity in this community, serving as the location for the Unity March. This plaza is the common link between all other entities, suggesting its significance in the community. The plaza's association with the march could potentially lead to issues such as public disorder or conflict, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. [Data: Entities (5), Relationships (37, 38, 39, 40, 41,+more)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Harmony Assembly's role in the community\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Harmony Assembly is another key entity in this community, being the organizer of the march at Verdant Oasis Plaza. The nature of Harmony Assembly and its march could be a potential source of threat, depending on their objectives and the reactions they provoke. The relationship between Harmony Assembly and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Entities(6), Relationships (38, 43)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Unity March as a significant event\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Unity March is a significant event taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza. This event is a key factor in the community's dynamics and could be a potential source of threat, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. The relationship between the march and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Relationships (39)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Tribune Spotlight\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity March taking place in Verdant Oasis Plaza. This suggests that the event has attracted media attention, which could amplify its impact on the community. The role of Tribune Spotlight could be significant in shaping public perception of the event and the entities involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n17,PACIENTES,\"PACIENTES refers to a diverse group of individuals facing various medical conditions that necessitate specialized nutritional support and dietary management. This group includes individuals suffering from chronic respiratory diseases such as EPOC (Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease), cystic fibrosis (FQ), and bronchiectasis (BQ), who often encounter nutritional challenges. Additionally, patients with celiac disease must adhere to a strict gluten-free diet and receive education about their condition and associated risks.\n\nCertain patients are at risk of refeeding syndrome, particularly those with a history of malnutrition, anorexia nervosa, or prolonged fasting, requiring careful monitoring and nutritional support. Others may need artificial nutrition at home due to an inability to meet their nutritional needs through regular food intake. This includes patients undergoing surgical procedures related to the digestive system, such as gastrostomy or jejunostomy, who require tailored nutritional support post-surgery.\n\nPACIENTES also encompasses individuals with food allergies or intolerances, who need appropriate information and treatment. Those suffering from conditions like dysphagia, particularly oropharyngeal dysphagia, face challenges in swallowing and require specialized care and management. This group includes patients receiving treatment in specialized units, such as the Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofaríngea, where their treatment and satisfaction are prioritized.\n\nFurthermore, patients with gastrointestinal disorders, such as Crohn's disease or ulcerative colitis, may require nutritional support to manage their conditions effectively. Individuals suffering from acute pancreatitis also undergo various treatments and nutritional assessments. \n\nIn the context of eating disorders, PACIENTES includes individuals with anorexia nervosa and bulimia nervosa, who face both psychological and nutritional challenges and require comprehensive dietary education and support. Additionally, patients with urea cycle disorders, who experience symptoms like hyperammonemia, necessitate dietary management and treatment.\n\nOverall, PACIENTES represents a broad spectrum of individuals requiring medical treatment and specialized nutritional care due to various health conditions, emphasizing the importance of individualized dietary plans and support systems tailored to their unique needs.\",227\r\n1752,UREA,\"UREA is a chemical compound that plays a significant role in assessing renal function and hydration status in patients. It is a waste product formed from the breakdown of proteins and is commonly measured in both blood and urine. In blood tests, urea levels are evaluated to determine kidney function and overall metabolic health, while in urine tests, it is used to calculate nitrogen balance. Additionally, urea is utilized in medical treatments to enhance the renal elimination of free water and reduce natriuresis, although it is noted for its poor palatability and issues with patient adherence.\",4\r\n6726,FÍSTULA PANCREÁTICA,\"FÍSTULA PANCREÁTICA is a medical complication that can arise following pancreatic surgery or as a result of pancreatitis. It is characterized by an abnormal connection between the pancreas and other organs, which leads to the leakage of pancreatic fluids. This condition can manifest as an external fistula with low to moderate output. The formation of a fistula is a pathological condition that poses significant health risks and requires careful management.\",3\r\n2094,MALNUTRICIÓN SEVERA,MALNUTRICIÓN SEVERA es una condición médica que puede señalar la necesidad de iniciar nutrición enteral o parenteral con el fin de restaurar el estado nutricional del paciente.,3\r\n8892,PSICOTERAPIA,\"PSICOTERAPIA es un tratamiento que implica la interacción entre un paciente y un terapeuta, utilizado para abordar trastornos psicológicos, incluyendo los trastornos de la conducta alimentaria. Este enfoque terapéutico es fundamental en el tratamiento de los trastornos alimentarios, ya que se centra en tratar los problemas psicológicos subyacentes y fomentar la recuperación del paciente.\",3\r\n8928,AN,\"AN, which stands for Anorexia Nervosa, is a type of eating disorder that significantly impacts dietary habits and caloric intake.\",2\r\n1265,HISTORIA CLÍNICA ELECTRÓNICA,\"The \"\"HISTORIA CLÍNICA ELECTRÓNICA\"\" (HCE) is an electronic health record system designed to store and manage comprehensive patient data. It includes the nutritional and medical history of patients, facilitating their ongoing monitoring and care. The HCE plays a crucial role in managing health conditions by providing vital information that supports healthcare professionals in making informed decisions regarding patient treatment and follow-up.\",2\r\n1862,VENTILACIÓN MECÁNICA,\"VENTILACIÓN MECÁNICA is a medical intervention that provides mechanical support for breathing in patients who are unable to breathe adequately on their own. This method is particularly important for individuals experiencing respiratory failure, as it assists or replaces spontaneous breathing. In certain cases, patients undergoing mechanical ventilation may also require enteral nutrition due to their inability to eat orally. This is especially relevant for premature newborns, who may be affected by their reliance on mechanical ventilation, impacting their capacity to receive enteral nutrition. Overall, VENTILACIÓN MECÁNICA serves as a critical support system for both respiration and nutritional needs in vulnerable patient populations.\",3\r\n5008,DENSITOMETRÍAS,\"DENSITOMETRÍAS refers to the practice of conducting bone density tests periodically to assess the health of bones, particularly in patients receiving parenteral nutrition. These tests are essential for monitoring the effects of parenteral nutrition on bone health, ensuring that any potential issues can be identified and addressed in a timely manner.\",2\r\n12617,REHABILITACIÓN MULTIMODAL,\"REHABILITACIÓN MULTIMODAL refers to a comprehensive set of post-surgical interventions designed to accelerate recovery and minimize complications following surgery. This approach incorporates various protocols, including early postoperative feeding, which is specifically aimed at enhancing the recovery process for patients.\",2\r\n12613,SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL POSTOPERATORIO,SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL POSTOPERATORIO refers to the nutritional support provided to patients after surgery to aid recovery.,2\r\n23,ENFERMEDADES NEUROLÓGICAS,\"\"\"ENFERMEDADES NEUROLÓGICAS\"\" refers to a range of disorders that significantly impact the nervous system and are a major health concern in developed countries. These diseases can lead to various complications, including altered consciousness and difficulties with swallowing, known as dysphagia. As a result, many patients suffering from neurological diseases may require artificial nutritional support, specifically enteral nutrition, to meet their dietary needs. Conditions such as Parkinson's disease, amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, and Alzheimer's disease are notable examples of neurological disorders that can severely impair the ability to eat normally, necessitating this form of nutritional intervention. Overall, neurological diseases present complex challenges that often require specialized care and support for affected individuals.\",5\r\n19,REHABILITACIÓN,\"Rehabilitación refers to the comprehensive process of rehabilitation that is often associated with enteral nutrition, aimed at helping patients regain their ability to eat orally. This process is particularly important for individuals suffering from oropharyngeal dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. Rehabilitation for oropharyngeal dysphagia involves the implementation of specific techniques and strategies designed to enhance swallowing safety and efficiency. The Rehabilitación (Rehabilitation) service is dedicated to the recovery and treatment of patients with various conditions, including those experiencing dysphagia. The Rehabilitation department provides targeted therapeutic interventions to improve the swallowing function of these patients, ensuring a holistic approach to their care and recovery.\",4\r\n4447,ADRENALINA,\"ADRENALINA, also known as adrenaline, is a hormone produced by the adrenal glands that plays a crucial role in the body's response to stress. It increases heart rate and enhances energy availability, which can be particularly important in emergency situations. The response to adrenaline can be affected by conditions such as hypothyroidism. Additionally, adrenaline is utilized as an emergency treatment for severe anaphylactic reactions, especially in patients with food allergies. It is essential for patients at risk of severe allergic reactions to have this medication readily available for self-administration in case of an emergency.\",3\r\n1587,ALIMENTACION ADAPTADA COMERCIAL,\"Commercially prepared food options that are adapted for individuals with swallowing difficulties, often in pureed form.\",2\r\n1586,ALIMENTACION ADAPTADA TRADICIONAL,\"Traditional adapted food designed for individuals with swallowing difficulties, typically in a pureed form.\",2\r\n12974,ALTERACIONES DEL METABOLISMO HIDROCARBONADO,\"Alterations in carbohydrate metabolism are common in cystic fibrosis patients, leading to complications such as diabetes.\",2\r\n850,CALIDAD ORGANOLÉPTICA,\"CALIDAD ORGANOLÉPTICA refers to the sensory quality attributes of food, which encompass taste, smell, appearance, and texture. These attributes are crucial for patient meals, as they significantly influence patient satisfaction in hospitals. Ensuring high calidad organoléptica in food served to patients is essential for enhancing their overall dining experience and well-being.\",2\r\n1192,EVALUACIÓN NUTRICIONAL,\"EVALUACIÓN NUTRICIONAL refers to the process of determining an individual's nutritional status through various measurements and analyses. This comprehensive evaluation is crucial for identifying dietary needs and nutritional support requirements, particularly for patients. It involves assessing a patient's dietary intake and overall nutritional status to ensure appropriate care is provided. This process is especially significant for individuals diagnosed with gastrointestinal cancers, as their nutritional needs may be more complex and require tailored interventions.\",2\r\n2488,ÍLEO GÁSTRICO,\"El íleo gástrico es una condición médica caracterizada por el retraso en el vaciamiento del estómago, frecuentemente observado en el periodo postoperatorio inmediato. Esta condición implica una obstrucción en el proceso de vaciamiento gástrico, lo que puede llevar a la necesidad de nutrición enteral para asegurar la adecuada ingesta de nutrientes.\",2\r\n5009,T-SCORE,\"T-SCORE is a measurement utilized in bone density tests to evaluate bone health. It serves as a comparative metric, assessing an individual's bone density against that of a healthy 30-year-old. Lower T-scores indicate a higher risk of osteoporosis, making it a crucial tool in diagnosing osteoporosis, particularly in patients with specific conditions such as FQ (cystic fibrosis).\",2\r\n6798,PADRES,\"The entity \"\"PADRES\"\" refers to parents who hold the responsibility of ensuring safe nutrition for their children with food allergies.\",2\r\n14564,TRAUMATISMO CRANEOENCEFÁLICO,\"Traumatismo craneoencefálico, or cranioencephalic trauma, refers to injuries affecting both the brain and skull. This type of traumatic brain injury can complicate enteral feeding processes and may lead to serious complications, necessitating immediate medical attention. Additionally, it can result in conditions such as SIADH (Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion), and the duration of treatment for such injuries can vary significantly. Overall, Traumatismo craneoencefálico represents a critical medical condition that requires prompt and effective management.\",2\r\n12464,TRAUMATISMOS,\"TRAUMATISMOS refer to severe physical injuries that necessitate medical attention and may benefit from immunomodulatory treatments. These injuries can impact the intestines, leading to conditions that require nutritional support, such as parenteral nutrition. Additionally, TRAUMATISMOS are recognized as one of the potential causes of type II intestinal failure, which may sometimes require extensive intestinal resections. In certain cases, surgical interventions, such as faringostomía, may be necessary to provide feeding access for affected individuals.\",2\r\n2656,PREMATURIDAD,\"Prematuridad is the condition of being born before the full term of pregnancy, often leading to various health challenges. This condition, known as prematurity, significantly impacts the nutritional needs of the infant, necessitating specific supplementation to support their development and health.\",2\r\n5328,PALADAR HENDIDO,\"Paladar Hendido, also known as cleft palate, is a congenital condition characterized by a malformation in the structure of the palate. This condition can significantly impact feeding, often necessitating the use of enteral nutrition to ensure adequate intake. Additionally, it has been noted that paladar hendido may occur in patients with hypogonadotropic hypogonadism, indicating a potential association with this hormonal condition.\",2\r\n1223,ALIMENTOS SEGUROS,The safe foods provided by the Servicio de Cocina Hospitalaria for the evaluation of dysphagia include yogurt and custard.,1\r\n2026,ALTO GRADO DE ESTRÉS METABÓLICO,\"Alto grado de estrés metabólico refers to a condition where the body's metabolic demands are significantly increased, often requiring careful nutritional management.\",1\r\n15429,ATRESIA ESOFÁGICA,\"Esophageal atresia is a congenital condition where the esophagus does not connect properly, necessitating enteral nutrition.\",1\r\n13016,ATROFIA MUSCULAR,\"Atrofia muscular, or muscle atrophy, is a condition characterized by the loss of muscle mass. This phenomenon is particularly prevalent in patients with ELA (Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis) as well as those suffering from chronic respiratory diseases. In these patients, muscle wasting can be attributed to a combination of factors, including nutritional deficiencies and increased energy requirements, which lead to inactivity. The condition highlights the importance of addressing both nutritional needs and physical activity to mitigate the effects of muscle atrophy in affected individuals.\",1\r\n5011,CALCEMIA,\"The level of calcium in the blood, which is crucial for diagnosing conditions related to bone health and vitamin D status.\",1\r\n11868,CIRROSIS DESCOMPENSADA,\"Decompensated cirrhosis is a severe liver condition that can develop in patients with Wilson's disease, leading to complications and potential transplantation.\",1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n473,PACIENTES,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,\"PACIENTES are individuals who may require NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL when enteral nutrition is insufficient or not possible due to various medical complications. This form of nutrition is specifically indicated for patients suffering from severe malnutrition, particularly when enteral nutrition cannot be administered. Patients receiving parenteral nutrition are those who cannot meet their nutritional needs through oral intake or other means, and they may also be recipients of home parenteral nutrition based on their specific medical conditions. Overall, parenteral nutrition serves as a critical alternative for patients who are unable to receive adequate nutrition through enteral routes.\",665\r\n445,PACIENTES,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,\"Enteral nutrition is a critical medical intervention utilized for patients who are unable to consume food orally due to various health conditions. This form of nutrition is particularly essential for patients undergoing procedures such as esophagectomy, as it supports their recovery process. Additionally, patients suffering from severe dysphagia are often recommended to receive enteral nutrition through a feeding tube to ensure they receive adequate nutrition and maintain their digestive health. Overall, patients are the primary recipients of enteral nutrition, which is designed to meet their specific dietary needs when oral intake is not feasible.\",562\r\n3286,PACIENTE,UREA,The patient's blood urea level was measured to evaluate kidney function,550\r\n3216,PACIENTE,FÍSTULA PANCREÁTICA,El paciente presenta una fístula pancreática que ha sido una complicación significativa en su tratamiento,549\r\n3090,PACIENTE,MALNUTRICIÓN SEVERA,Un paciente que presenta malnutrición severa puede requerir nutrición enteral o parenteral para mejorar su estado nutricional,549\r\n3459,PACIENTE,PSICOTERAPIA,El paciente puede recibir psicoterapia como parte de su tratamiento para abordar los aspectos psicológicos de los trastornos de la conducta alimentaria.,549\r\n3467,PACIENTE,AN,Los pacientes con AN requieren atención médica especializada y soporte nutricional para su recuperación,548\r\n3305,PACIENTE,HISTORIA CLÍNICA ELECTRÓNICA,La historia clínica electrónica contiene información sobre la historia nutricional del paciente,548\r\n4807,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,FÍSTULA PANCREÁTICA,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL may be used in the management of FÍSTULA PANCREÁTICA when enteral nutrition is not possible,441\r\n4645,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,VENTILACIÓN MECÁNICA,Patients requiring ventilación mecánica often need nutrición parenteral to meet their nutritional needs during treatment.,441\r\n4965,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,DENSITOMETRÍAS,Bone density tests are important for monitoring the effects of parenteral nutrition on bone health.,440\r\n294,DISFAGIA,PACIENTES,\"Dysphagia is a condition that significantly impacts patients, particularly those with specific health issues such as esophageal cancer and cerebrovascular disease. Patients with esophageal cancer experience dysphagia, which severely affects their ability to eat and can lead to nutritional deficiencies. Similarly, patients with cerebrovascular disease frequently suffer from dysphagia, hindering their capacity to feed themselves properly. This condition poses considerable challenges for patients, as they often struggle with swallowing, which can compromise their nutritional status and overall health. To address these challenges, many patients with dysphagia may require enteral nutrition to ensure they receive adequate nutrient intake. Overall, dysphagia is a critical concern for patients, necessitating medical attention and intervention to manage their dietary needs effectively.\",380\r\n2827,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,VENTILACIÓN MECÁNICA,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL y VENTILACIÓN MECÁNICA son dos entidades interrelacionadas en el contexto del cuidado de pacientes, especialmente en recién nacidos prematuros. La ventilación mecánica puede complicar la administración de nutrición enteral en estos pacientes, lo que a menudo requiere ajustes en su alimentación para asegurar que reciban los nutrientes necesarios. Por otro lado, en situaciones donde los pacientes no pueden alimentarse por vía oral debido a su condición médica, la ventilación mecánica puede hacer necesario el uso de nutrición enteral como una alternativa para garantizar su nutrición adecuada. En resumen, la interacción entre la nutrición enteral y la ventilación mecánica es crucial en el manejo de la alimentación de pacientes con dificultades respiratorias y de deglución.\",338\r\n2751,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,REHABILITACIÓN MULTIMODAL,Rehabilitación multimodal includes nutritional support as part of the recovery process,337\r\n2745,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL POSTOPERATORIO,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL is a key component of SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL POSTOPERATORIO for recovery,337\r\n586,PACIENTES,MALNUTRICIÓN,\"Los pacientes, especialmente aquellos con cáncer de esófago, a menudo enfrentan problemas de malnutrición. Esta condición se debe principalmente a la pérdida de peso y a la disminución de la ingesta de alimentos. Además, los pacientes que están en riesgo de síndrome de realimentación también experimentan malnutrición, lo que agrava su estado de salud. En conjunto, estas situaciones resaltan la vulnerabilidad de los pacientes a la malnutrición, que puede ser un factor crítico en su tratamiento y recuperación.\",331\r\n478,PACIENTES,DESNUTRICIÓN,\"The entity \"\"PACIENTES\"\" refers to individuals who may experience \"\"DESNUTRICIÓN,\"\" a condition characterized by inadequate nutrition. Patients suffering from desnutrición require careful monitoring and nutritional intervention to restore their health. In some cases, this may necessitate the administration of parenteral nutrition, which is a method of delivering nutrients directly into the bloodstream, bypassing the digestive system. Overall, addressing desnutrición in patients is crucial for their recovery and overall well-being.\",301\r\n499,PACIENTES,VITAMINA D,\"Patients on home parenteral nutrition often require monitoring and supplementation of vitamin D, as this vitamin plays a crucial role in their overall health. Additionally, vitamin D levels are associated with the health outcomes of patients suffering from chronic respiratory diseases, indicating its importance in managing these conditions. Therefore, maintaining adequate vitamin D levels is essential for both patients on home parenteral nutrition and those with chronic respiratory issues to support their health and improve their outcomes.\",301\r\n596,PACIENTES,CÁNCER,\"The entity \"\"PACIENTES\"\" refers to individuals who are diagnosed with \"\"CÁNCER\"\" and are in need of nutritional treatment. These patients often suffer from anorexia, a common symptom associated with cancer, which can lead to difficulties in maintaining adequate nutrition. As a result, they may require enteral nutrition to support their dietary needs during treatment.\",293\r\n491,PACIENTES,PROTEÍNAS,Proteins are a critical component of the dietary needs for patients,284\r\n658,PACIENTES,ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL,Patients with inflammatory bowel disease may need enteral nutrition to maintain proper nutrition,284\r\n551,PACIENTES,PANCREATITIS AGUDA,Patients are diagnosed with acute pancreatitis and receive treatment,281\r\n522,PACIENTES,ZINC,\"Zinc deficiency is common among patients with eating disorders, and its supplementation can improve recovery outcomes\",279\r\n521,PACIENTES,HIERRO,\"Patients with eating disorders often experience iron deficiency, which can complicate their recovery\",272\r\n507,PACIENTES,CIRUGÍA BARIÁTRICA,Los pacientes con obesidad pueden requerir cirugía bariátrica para tratar su condición,268\r\n528,PACIENTES,DIABETES MELLITUS TIPO 2,Pacientes are individuals diagnosed with diabetes mellitus tipo 2 who require ongoing management and education,267\r\n423,UNIDAD FUNCIONAL DE DISFAGIA OROFARÍNGEA,PACIENTES,\"The Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofaríngea is dedicated to providing specialized care for patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia, a condition that affects their ability to swallow. This unit focuses on the treatment of swallowing disorders, ensuring that patients receive comprehensive care tailored to their needs. The primary goal of the Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofaríngea is to enhance patient satisfaction while effectively addressing the challenges associated with dysphagia.\",263\r\n648,PACIENTES,ALBUMINA,Los niveles de albúmina en los pacientes se utilizan para evaluar su estado nutricional y pueden influir en la natremia,257\r\n584,PACIENTES,PÉRDIDA DE PESO,Los pacientes con cáncer de esófago a menudo experimentan pérdida de peso significativa.,254\r\n530,PACIENTES,HIPERTRIGLICERIDEMIA,Patients with Glycogen Storage Disease I may have elevated triglyceride levels as a result of their dietary management and metabolic issues.,251\r\n625,PACIENTES,HIPERCALCEMIA,Patients with hypercalcemia may have specific dietary restrictions that affect enteral nutrition,251\r\n505,PACIENTES,IMC,\"The Body Mass Index (IMC) is a critical tool used to evaluate the nutritional status of patients, particularly those with specific health conditions such as cancer and MELAS. In the context of cancer patients, the IMC is employed to assess their nutritional status prior to surgery, ensuring that they are in optimal health for the procedure. Similarly, for patients with MELAS, low IMC values are indicative of a risk of malnutrition, highlighting the importance of monitoring their nutritional health. Overall, the assessment of patients' nutritional status through IMC is essential for effective health management across various medical conditions.\",250\r\n570,PACIENTES,DIABETES TIPO 2,Patients with chronic respiratory diseases are at increased risk of developing type 2 diabetes due to various factors,250\r\n592,PACIENTES,QUIMIOTERAPIA,\"Los pacientes con cáncer a menudo reciben quimioterapia, lo que puede afectar su nutrición\",250\r\n578,PACIENTES,CÁNCER GÁSTRICO,Los pacientes son los que padecen cáncer gástrico y requieren tratamiento nutricional para mejorar su pronóstico,249\r\n571,PACIENTES,SÍNDROME METABÓLICO,\"Patients with chronic respiratory diseases may exhibit components of metabolic syndrome, affecting their overall health\",248\r\n56